# ── test: LiteSVM-only fixture used by ./test.sh — NEVER deployable ──
# This is not a runtime environment: it is the set of values baked into the
# committed source so the unit-test suite can run against a fixed, signable
# build on a throwaway in-memory chain.
#
# PROGRAM_ID — pinned by hand and permanent: it is the pubkey of the keypair
# `anchor build` generated when the project was created, and it must equal
# `declare_id!` in src/lib.rs, because the tests load the built binary at
# exactly this address inside LiteSVM. Never deployed to a real cluster.
PROGRAM_ID=GowYj1dH8kM9sD88cEFk8PExCkct7AqLWGvTkWz6evoD

# PULLER_KEYS — three entries, two origins:
#   1. D8BX…  — the real Mesh puller key (private key in the backend's Key
#      Vault), listed so a locally-run backend can also sign in test setups.
#   2+3. AKnL… / 9hSR… — test-only keys the LiteSVM suite signs with. Their
#      private keys are DERIVED FROM PUBLIC SEEDS ([1u8;32] / [2u8;32] — see
#      fixture_puller_keypairs in tests/test_controller.rs), so anyone can
#      reproduce them. Safe on LiteSVM's throwaway chain — and exactly why a
#      test build must never reach a real cluster.
PULLER_KEYS="D8BXX8NxgxFN9LifSuDYQ8rTBfd9wfzVAL1KrntMBnU1 AKnL4NNf3DGWZJS6cPknBuEGnVsV4A4m5tgebLHaRSZ9 9hSR6S7WPtxmTojgo6GG3k4yDPecgJY292j7xrsUGWBu"
